## GS_POWERSCHOOL — Goldman Sachs, "Project Picasso – Board of Directors Discussion Materials" (Mar-2024), 13.33×7.5, 35 pp

**Frame**
- Title: very large bold navy (#0C2454-ish, GS navy), ~28–32 pt equivalent, left at fx 0.05, fy 0.07; titles often wrap to 2 lines (GS accepts 2-line titles, Title Case, statement-style: "Sponsors Remained Most Active Buyers", "Software Multiples Have Adjusted to a New Reality").
- GS logo box top-right (fx 0.88–0.94), red italic "Confidential" above it.
- Thick navy bar along the very bottom edge (full width, ~1.2% of height). Page "Investment Banking | 7" grey, bottom-right.
- Source + Note block: italic 9–10 pt, bottom-left, "Source: FactSet; market data as of 1-Jan-2024" then "Note: …" with superscript footnotes ¹ ² — every data slide has it.
- Section dividers: full light-grey (#F0F0F0) slide, bold navy title left-middle, navy tab "Investment Banking" bottom-right with light-blue end cap. Very plain.
- Agenda: 4 numbered rows — navy filled circle with white number + light-blue (#D6E8F7) full-width bar with bold navy text. (Same family as FEMSA roman pills.)

**Executive summary (p3)**: tagline box on top (cream/yellow #FCF6DA fill + thin navy outline, bold italic centered sentence) → 2 square-bullet level-1 statements (bold-ish) each with 3–5 em-dash sub-bullets. Text only. Reading order: framing banner → claim → evidence dashes.

**Chart slides — GS chart grammar**
- p6 (stacked column + logos): chart header = centered bold navy text with thin navy rule ("Sponsor % of Software M&A Volume (excl. Deals Over $20bn)"); **a KPI row above the bars** (37% 40% 39%… in bold on a light band) aligned to each column — a "metric strip" above the chart; stacked columns (navy dark = sponsors, light blue = strategics, red = deals >$20bn with **company logos inside the red segment**); totals ($130, $59…) bold above; segment labels white inside; red outside labels for the top segment value; **rounded callout boxes with leader lines** ("64 Strategic Transactions"); second metric strip below ("Number of Sponsor Take-Privates": 8 2 10 6 …); then **two logo-tombstone panels** (rounded outline boxes) at bottom with deal size + date under each logo. Very dense, layered: metric strip → chart → metric strip → logo panels → source.
- p7: 3 small-multiple column charts side by side, each with a centered bold header + underline (Sponsors / Strategics <$10bn / Strategics >$10bn), different color per panel (orange, light blue, navy); **dashed average lines per year with colored labels "2021 Average: $23"**; big diagonal arrow drawn over the chart to show trend; red-filled translucent highlight box on the last period with logo callout.
- p8: dual-axis line chart (3 series navy / light blue / purple), header + **light-blue banner box with the takeaway sentence inside the chart area**; orange dashed rectangle highlighting the recent period; end-of-line value labels in series color at right; legend bottom.
- p9: long time-series line chart (4 series) + **embedded mini-table inside the chart's empty upper-left** (3Y Avg / Current / COVID Avg) colored by series; end labels right.
- p11/p13: indexed performance lines + **mini performance table top-right with the key column outlined by a red dashed box and yellow fill** (Since IPO). End-of-line labels with % in series color. Series colors: Picasso light blue, peers navy/grey, index dark red.
- p12: price line (navy, thick) + horizontal reference lines for 52-week high (light blue) / low (purple) with labels; dashed-outline mini table (Daily avg volume); **right side VWAP stack table** (label / value, current price row highlighted cream, "vs. current" italic rows in green/red).
- p14: analyst table (zebra light blue) + highlighted median row (cream/orange band) + **vertical light-blue side label box** ("Median price target implies 30% upside") + 2 mini charts below (price vs target line; stacked rating bars).
- p26/p35: precedent premia — full-width single-color navy column chart sorted descending, dashed median/percentile lines with colored labels at right; **data table directly under each bar** (announcement date / target / acquirer / value / % cash / premium) aligned to bar columns. "Chart-as-table-header" pattern.
- p27 (Analysis at various prices — AVP): navy header row with price columns; italic label rows; Enterprise value row on light-blue band + bold; **purple dots with tiny labels marking benchmark positions inside the grid** (e.g., "Software median 30%"); the recommended price range boxed by a **pink dashed vertical rectangle** spanning the table.
- p32: league-table grid (navy cell = GS, grey others) + 2 bar charts with GS bar navy, others very light blue, **dashed rounded callout "46% above #2"**.

**Box / shape vocabulary (GS)**
- Rounded-corner rectangles everywhere for content panels (p16, p17, p19, p24 logos) with thin outline in the panel color, often with a soft drop shadow (GS uses shadow on panels — unlike Aztlan).
- Header strips: full-width filled bar (navy / purple / orange / light blue) with white bold text on top of a white panel (p17 "Expansion in India", "International Leadership").
- Investment highlights (p16): left = stack of 9 rounded-outline pill rows (bold navy text, each pill outlined; 3 colored outlines highlight the ones expanded later) ; right = 2×2 grid of **solid colored tiles with a white line icon + bold white caption** (purple, orange, navy, light blue). This is the main place GS uses icons.
- Subtitle banner: light-blue (#D6E8F7) box with navy outline + bold centered sentence directly under the title (p17, p18, p19) = the "so-what".
- Big KPI boxes (p19): outlined rectangle with large bold italic number "107%" + caption.
- Option comparison (p23): 3 column heads with numbered circles; **row labels as colored filled blocks at left** (navy, steel blue, purple, orange, yellow, dark red) ; content cells with "+" (pro, red plus) and "–" (con) bullets; check marks ✓✓✓ for scoring rows; the recommended column has **yellow fill + dark-red dashed border** and a tag "GS Recommendation" (dashed box) above.
- Timeline/Gantt (p28): navy year header, month/week grid, purple filled bars, ★ for milestones, bracket annotations "~3 weeks".
- Buyer lists (p25): vertical rotated-text color bars at left grouping tiers (Tier 1 navy, Strategics light blue, Tier 2 purple, Tier 3 orange, Likely not interested green) + logo + contact + fund size table.
- Credentials: tombstone grid (8×3 outlined boxes: logo, role, deal, logo, date) p33; "advisor of choice" (p30) = 4 columns of icon + big number + caption separated by dashed vertical lines and "+" signs, with faded logo cloud background.
- Images: **only logos, product screenshots (p18 framed in rounded cards), and maps (p17)**. No photos of people/places. Images serve as evidence ("Picasso AI in products today") or identity (logos).

**Palette** navy #0C2454/#0A3254, light blue #D6E8F7/#9DBBE0, mid blue #6E9BCB, purple #6B1F6E, orange #F39200, dark red #A6192E, cream highlight #FCF6DA, greys. Font: a humanist sans (GS Sans-like), bold titles.

