## BARC_NUVEI — Barclays, "Project Neon – Board Materials" (Apr-2024), 9.72×7.52 (≈4:3), 25 pp — fairness/valuation board book

**Frame**: Title Arial-like bold black ~24 pt, top-left (fx 0.06, fy 0.08), one line, **topic-style (noun phrase)** not action sentence ("Transaction Background", "Neon Valuation Summary"). Footer: thin light-blue rule full width at fy 0.93, page number left under it, BARCLAYS logo right. No subtitle.
Cover & dividers: **cyan field (#00AEEF) with a big white inset rectangle** (white "card" with ~8% cyan margin) containing title bold black left-aligned; logo eagle top-right on cyan. Dividers same frame, title only.
- Notice "All currencies stated in USD ($) throughout materials" in red italic top-right (p4) — currency disclaimer convention.

**Signature element: the full-width blue header bar** (#1E64C8-ish royal blue, white bold centered 11–12 pt, h ≈ 3.5% of height) sitting right under the title above every exhibit ("Analysis at Various Prices (Mgmt. Projections)", "Neon Stock Price Performance Since IPO"). When there are two exhibits, each gets its own bar (half width). Secondary header bars in **teal (#14A39A)** for second-type exhibits (Transaction Multiples, Peers, Adj. EBITDA Margin). Sub-headers in **light cyan bars** (#29B6F6-ish) with white text (Management Plan / Consensus / Delta in dark grey).
- Rotated vertical side tabs (cyan/grey filled, white rotated text "Summary Value", "Premiums", "Multiples", "Valuation", "Reference") grouping rows of a table or football field. Same idea as GS tier bars.

**Slide patterns**
- Text slides (p4, p5): plain round-bullet lists, 11–12 pt, sub-bullets square; p5 separates parties with **thin blue horizontal rules** between blocks (no boxes).
- AVP table (p6): columns per offer price, each offer column enclosed in **red dashed vertical box**; final offer column solid blue outline; row groups with side tabs; italic % rows; bold totals; parentheses negatives.
- Stock chart with event annotations (p8): single cyan price line; shaded hatched vertical bands for periods (Covid, short-seller report) with grey label tabs; **dashed-outline callout boxes with leader lines** for events (earnings = yellow dashed, acquisitions = grey dashed, media leak = red dashed — legend at bottom explains box types); horizontal dashed 52W high/low lines with colored labels at right end; **market-statistics box top-right** (thin blue outline, small table: price, shares, equity value, EV bridge); **summary strip below the chart** (blue outlined box: 30-day avg / 1Y / 2Y / 3Y / 52W high/low with premiums).
- Indexed lines (p9): 2 stacked charts each with a header bar + a small navy-header table at the top-right corner (Annual returns / Average multiples by year).
- Management plan (p10): left big financial table (light-blue bands on key rows, CAGR column at right boxed, dashed vertical line separating actual vs projected), right column = 3 stacked "KPI target" panels each: teal header bar → grey box with italic "Target: 15–20% growth" → small cyan column chart. Text→target→evidence chart.
- Mgmt vs consensus (p11): grouped column headers (colored bars per group), delta columns shaded grey hatch for N/A.
- Numbered list slide (p13): 5 wide light-grey gradient bars, big blue number left, blue bold text — the "steps / changes" list.
- p14: valuation bridge columns: unadjusted (light) vs adjusted (dark) bars per period, with **red dashed boxes "Δ of (0.5x)" + red arrows** pointing to change. Teal for transaction multiples, blue for trading.
- **Football field (p15)** — canonical: header bar "Price per Share"; left labels grouped under bold category labels (Comparable Companies / Precedent Transactions / DCF) with side tab "Valuation" (cyan) and "Reference" (grey) separated by a **dashed cyan horizontal line**; navy horizontal floating bars for valuation methods, **light grey bars for reference items** (LBO, premiums, analyst targets, 52-week range) with ◆ marker for median/avg; low/high values printed at each bar end; **vertical dashed reference lines** for unaffected price (red dashed label box) and offer price (blue dashed label box) labelled at top; x-axis share price at bottom with a small implied multiples table under the axis (Premium, EV, EV/EBITDA rows). Right column: "Assumptions" header bar + stacked outlined boxes with bold method name + 2 bullets each (multiple ranges in bold).
- Benchmarking (p16): 4 panels of horizontal bar charts side by side, logos as row labels at left (shared), subject company bars cyan, peers navy, dashed-outline boxes for comparison values; group side-tabs ("Business comps", "Business + Valuation comps"); median rows at bottom in dashed boxes. Break symbol "//" on outlier bar.
- Precedents (p17): dense table with header bar, side tab "Post market peak", quartile/median/mean summary block bottom-right in bold.
- DCF (p18): top = projection table (historicals grey header, projections teal header, CAGR column) ; bottom-left "Equity Value Build" (header + cyan pill with assumptions "@ 10.75x exit / 14.25% WACC" + $/per share/% table); bottom-right "Sensitivity Analysis" = 4 mini 3×3 grids (WACC rows × multiple / growth cols) with rotated "WACC" label.
- WACC (p21): 2 tables side by side, key rows boxed, **dashed box + arrow to "Average: 13.5%" callout** (lavender dashed pill).
- Premiums paid (p23): subtitle sentence in bold under title; small column charts (quartiles) under teal/blue header bars; logo pairs table (target / acquirer).
- Analyst targets (p24): table + histogram of price targets (teal columns, count labels above).

**Shapes**: square corners everywhere (Barclays = rectangles, header bars, dashed boxes). Rounded only for small pills. No icons, no photos. Logos only as table row labels.
**Palette**: cyan #00AEEF (brand), royal blue #0B5ED7/#1F6FD1, navy #0A2D5C, teal #12A19A/#0E8C82, light cyan fills #E3F4FD, grey #D9D9D9, red only for dashed highlight boxes. Font Arial/Helvetica.

